Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.39.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.39.0 (archive 38 conclusion applied): the log proved that ABOVE A FULL-SCREEN APP the float's CONTENT (a hosted FBScene layer) still receives touches while its surrounding grab bars (plain SpringBoard views) do not, and that the screen EDGE region still receives them (the status-bar mirror hot strip fired 3 times). Grabbing therefore moved to the edge: (1) a right-edge PICKUP BAND (56x300, in both the standalone zone window and the mirrored status-bar window) where a one-finger vertical/diagonal drag MOVES the float window and a distinct leftward swipe (>30pt) reveals the arc picker, while a TWO-finger vertical drag resizes the float proportionally around its centre - so the float can be moved and resized even while another app is full-screen; (2) the arc picker is now Pinned in place as requested - the arc centre is fixed at the vertical middle of the screen once revealed and only the highlight follows the finger, releasing over an icon opens that app in the float and releasing over empty space closes the picker; (3) gesture disambiguation is deferred until 6pt of movement (30pt for the picker swipe) so a drag never pops the picker accidentally.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
